/code-review high — U5 round 1 — branch 2026-09-25-gate-hardening (develop...HEAD, wave 1: U1–U4)

1. plugins/stackgen/stacks/toolchain-manager/mise/config/.config/mise.toml:164 — The linter pin "npm:@askviraj/linter" = "1.1.6" is refused by a default mise install because the package gets too few downloads; nothing in the shipped config allows it.
   Failure: reproduced with mise 2026.9.12 in a clean HOME and data dir: `mise install npm:@askviraj/linter@1.1.6` fails with "aube install failed: refusing to add @askviraj/linter: only 29 weekly downloads (threshold: 1000) ... set `allow_low_downloads = true`". The pin is in the base [tools] every shaped repo gets, so mise install (bootstrap, setup:all, CI with locked=true) exits non-zero in every repo. The maintainer's machine hides this because both its global config and this repo's .config/mise.toml set npm.package_manager = "pnpm". { version = "1.1.6", allow_low_downloads = true } installs cleanly (verified).

2. plugins/stackgen/stacks/toolchain-manager/mise/config/.config/mise.toml:164 — The linter is installed in every repo, but its binary runs node, and swift, swiftui, flutter, python and blank repos pin no node, so code:lint breaks there.
   Failure: reproduced: after installing with allow_low_downloads, `mise x -- linter --version` with PATH=/usr/bin:/bin fails with ".bin/linter: line 18: exec: node: not found". flutter code:lint (line 99) and swift/swiftui code:lint (line 198) call linter unconditionally, so the lint gate and its pre-commit hook fail on any machine without a global node. ruff and the default mise code:lint never call the linter but still install it. The pin belongs with a node pin, or in the packs whose code:lint calls it.

3. plugins/stackgen/stacks/package-manager/pnpm/config/.config/mise/tasks/code/format:98 — The leading-dash fix covers dprint only. shfmt (all six format tasks) and ruff format still get raw staged names, and the new comment "Every path is handed over prefixed ./" is false for the rest of the task.
   Failure: stage -x.sh; shell_files_in_scope passes it unprefixed; `shfmt -d -i 2 -ci -x.sh` exits 2 with "flag provided but not defined: -x.sh" (reproduced, shfmt 3.14.1). Format hook fails, commit blocked. In ruff, a staged -x.py reaches `uv run ruff format --check -x.py` (ruff/code/format:106). Prefixing files once at the top of each task, or inside shell_files_in_scope, fixes every tool.

